{"availability":"available","full":"nunchux-ai/nunchaku","name":"nunchaku","description":"[ICLR2025 Spotlight] SVDQuant: Absorbing Outliers by Low-Rank Components for 4-Bit Diffusion Models","category":"AI & machine learning","language":"Python","stars":3960,"forks":283,"created":"2024-11-06T07:24:40Z","updated":"2026-09-06T23:07:26Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"nunchux.ai","topics":["comfyui","diffusion-models","flux","genai","iclr","iclr2025","lora","mlsys","quantization"],"demo":"https://nunchux.ai/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:59.143Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:59.143Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T17:00:59.143Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:05:52.904Z","stars":3959,"forks":280},{"at":"2026-10-11T00:25:13.564Z","stars":3959,"forks":280},{"at":"2026-10-15T17:00:59.143Z","stars":3960,"forks":283}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Nunchaku is a high-performance inference engine optimized for 4-bit neural networks, as introduced in our paper SVDQuant. For the underlying quantization library, check out DeepCompressor.","Nunchaku is a high-performance inference engine for low-bit neural networks. It implements SVDQuant, a post-training quantization technique for 4-bit weights and activations that well maintains visual fidelity. On 12B FLUX.1-dev, it achieves 3.6× memory reduction compared to the BF16 model. By eliminating CPU offloading, it offers 8.7× speedup over the 16-bit model when on a 16GB laptop 4090 GPU, 3× faster than the NF4 W4A16 baseline. On PixArt-∑, it demonstrates significantly superior visual quality over other W4A4 or even W4A8 baselines. \"E2E\" means the end-to-end latency including the text…","SVDQuant: Absorbing Outliers by Low-Rank Components for 4-Bit Diffusion Models"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/nunchux-ai/nunchaku/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d8abacaeb29519eb76e6dc6ccc926b4cc81261a8a723d06c5e88bc